      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(minimax): persist OAuth model context metadata",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nMiniMax Portal OAuth login previously persisted an empty `models.providers.minimax-portal.models` array. That left status/context resolution without the OAuth model metadata and could produce `? / 400k` instead of MiniMax M3's native 1,000,000-token context window.\n\n## Fix\n\nPersist `buildMinimaxPortalProvider().models` in the OAuth config patch and update the existing regression assertion.\n\nThis is intentionally limited to:\n- `extensions/minimax/provider-registration.ts`\n- `extensions/minimax/index.test.ts`\n\n## Evidence\n\nFocused validation on the rebased branch:\n- `node_modules/.bin/vitest run extensions/minimax/index.test.ts` (14 passed)\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check extensions/minimax/index.test.ts extensions/minimax/provider-registration.ts`\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxlint --tsconfig config/tsconfig/oxlint.extensions.json extensions/minimax/index.test.ts extensions/minimax/provider-registration.ts`\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n\nLive verification against a real local MiniMax Portal OAuth setup, with credentials redacted:\n```\nOAuth profile: minimax-portal:default\nOAuth type/status: oauth / ok\nLive probe: minimax-portal/MiniMax-M3, status=ok, maxTokens=1\nConfigured model: minimax-portal/MiniMax-M3\nConfigured context window: 1000000\nSession listing: MiniMax-M3 ... 27k/1000k (3%)\n```\n\nThe branch was refreshed onto official `main` at `b34d0a8bb6aa`.\n\nThe full CI run also exposes an unrelated upstream baseline error at `src/security/audit-extra.async.ts:196` (`Cannot find name 'fs'`), which causes the type/lint/package-boundary shards to fail.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nExisting OAuth credentials and provider ids are unchanged. The patch only preserves model metadata that was already available in the bundled MiniMax catalog.\n",
        "branch": "fix/minimax-oauth-context-window",
